{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the archives was thick with the scent of old parchment and something sharper—the metallic tang of ozone that always preceded a surge in the Ember. Elara moved through the stacks, her footsteps swallowed by the heavy velvet rugs. The Codex sat on its pedestal, pulsing with a low, rhythmic light that seemed to sync with her own heartbeat. It wasn't just a book; it was a living thing, and tonight, it was restless.

She reached out, her fingers hovering just inches from the leather binding. The heat radiating from the pages was palpable, a dry warmth that made the fine hairs on her arms stand up. "Just one look," she whispered to the empty hall. "Just one page to see if the legends are true."

As her skin brushed the cover, the shadows in the corners of the room began to stretch and coil, dancing to the rhythm of the Codex's glow. The Ember wasn't just waking; it was reaching out.", "book_id": "01a02b5b-9a6d-796a-8dd1-e8fa7e4d98ba", "chapter": "1", "chapter_id": "01a02b5b-9b09-726b-8f3c-5319670d3154"}, "tier": "A"}

